# ── Never commit the dataset or the audio ────────────────────────────────
# The corpus is ~5.4 GB of wav files and the manifests run to tens of
# thousands of rows. GitHub rejects files over 100 MB and a repository this
# size becomes unusable to clone. Keep the audio on shared storage and the
# manifests wherever your team keeps data; the scripts find them by path.
combined/
dataset/
audio/
*.wav
*.mp3
*.flac
dataset_v*.csv
metadata*.csv
manifest*.csv

# ── Run output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The whole results folder: a run writes a CSV, a report, a status file and a
# clock file into it after every sample. None of it belongs in the repository,
# and listing them one pattern at a time missed new ones as they were added.
results/
ci_output/
*.elapsed.json
results_detailed*.csv
full_metrics_*.csv
batch_results_*.csv
report_*.xlsx
summary*.json
smartscribe_asr_eval_*.txt
batch_*_size*.txt
status.json
*.elapsed.json
status.json.tmp
stop.request
run.log
run_*.json

